  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I verified TX-0401 in account ACC-1005:\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Type:** Card payment, outgoing\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nI also see TX-0402, dated 2026-07-14, with the same merchant and the same amount (EUR 240.00). That is factual, but it doesn't tell us whether anything went wrong.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes available to you, and what each would cover:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** You were charged more than once for the same purchase. TX-0401 and TX-0402 would fit this pattern if they are two charges for one order.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** You did not authorize the payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** Your card details were used without your permission for an online or phone payment.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid, but the goods were never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid, but the service was never provided.\n\nWhich of these applies depends on what happened. Tell me, and I will check whether a dispute can be opened under that code before taking any action. I will not open anything without your confirmation.",
